# wear/man/jerkin: the man's jerkin (hunter, woodsman, some farmers): a sleeveless leather jerkin laced up the front over
# his shirt (the shirt's colour at the shoulders, in the lacing and down the arms with the archer's bracers), a dark
# belt with a brass buckle and a pouch on the left hip, short split tabs to the hip; a seamed back
# GARB-M (P2b wave 2); fitted to the man (STYLE_P2 22). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# The side run (leg pass round 2, 2026-10-20): the side `run` views are the rest views with the first row under the
# belt dropped, so the hem rides a row up while running (the skirt flaring) and the legs show under it as limbs.
# PROTO6 i3 (2026-10-22; the blind panel: the run read as an upright walk): each side `run` view has a `runl` twin that
# the side run frames name (loco.clip torso=runl): the rows from 4 under the neck sit a pixel back and from 7 under it two
# pixels back, so under the clip's lean 4 the chest leads the waist (a real lean; the head never leaves the torso) and the
# hem lands where lean 2 put it, over the run legs; the hip-anchored tails follow it (hip 2, the woman's 3). Walks keep `run`.
use person
body man
role garment jerkin
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso

